scope: |
  rozum, fourth instance of one shape: a method the walker has no lowering for is emitted as a
  VERBATIM Rust method call -- `xs.indexOf(...)`, `xs.zipWithIndex` -- so rustc blames the user's
  code for something the backend could not do. They report the SHAPE, not just three names, and
  their slice needs ~33 more of the same class.
  Two halves, and the second is the one that generalises:
    1. lower the methods (indexOf/find/zipWithIndex and what else the same probe shows);
    2. an unknown method on a receiver we KNOW is a Vec/String must be a refusal naming it.
  Conservative on (2): a pass-through is legitimate for a user's own type, so refusing must be
  scoped to receivers whose type the walker actually knows.
next: reproduce their three, then find what else their slice needs
